+/// TF_DS_PAIR_BROKEN: what rank 0 does once the pair cannot go on (a follower ended or stopped answering, a KV
+/// transfer failed across parts or timed out, the ranks' spill/KV-shard command streams diverged). `exit`: the lane
+/// host admits nothing more, fails what waits, lets decoding streams finish within its bound (or fails them when the
+/// device stream is wedged), aborts the NCCL communicator and exits with LaneHost.pair_exit_code, so the service's
+/// watchdog (or systemd) restarts both ranks; the communicator cannot be rebuilt in place. `degrade`: the old
+/// behaviour (requests fail one by one, the spill tier stops writing and restoring, the watchdog decides). Unset:
+/// `exit` with the spill tier or TF_DS_KV_SHARD on, else `degrade` (nothing changes with both off).
+pub const PairMode = enum { degrade, exit };
